# The life-assistant descriptor, shared by every instance. Deployment comes from
# plow-pbc/agent-mgr; this file carries only what is true for ALL of them.
#
# Note what is NOT here: AGENT_HOME, AGENT_CONTAINER and AGENT_PROJECT. Those are
# derived by agent-mgr from the REGISTRY NAME, which is what lets `life` and
# `rowan` run from this one checkout with separate homes and containers.
# Declaring any of them would pin every instance to one, and agent-mgr's
# ownership guard would then refuse every instance but that one -- it accepts a
# home only when it matches the instance's own name. The silence is the feature.

# No AGENT_TZ. It is per-person, and a shared descriptor can hold only ONE
# value -- so shipping a zone here gives it to EVERY instance. This repo carried
# America/Chicago while it served one person; keeping it once the repo is shared
# would boot the operator's instance on someone else's clock, two hours wrong in
# exactly the place a life assistant exists for.
#
# So instances take agent-mgr's fleet default (America/Los_Angeles) until
# plow-pbc/agent-mgr#14 adds a per-instance overlay. An instance whose owner is
# NOT Pacific must not be registered until it lands: `rowan` needs
# America/Chicago and is deliberately still on its pre-agent-mgr deployment,
# which supplies that zone from its own compose file.

# Where the declarative config lives, relative to this repo. True of every
# instance, so it belongs here.
AGENT_CONFIG=runtime/config.yaml
